@startuml DomainModel
' ===========================================================================
' POS System - Domain Model (conceptual classes, NO operations)
' Software Engineering Practice - Part 2, artifact 2  (= OOA)
'
' Conceptual perspective only: these are real-world things in the shop,
' not software objects.  No method signatures appear, by definition of a
' Domain Model (see Applying UML and Patterns, section 9.2).
' ===========================================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 26
skinparam ranksep 36
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FDFDF5
  BorderColor #7F6000
  ArrowColor #7F6000
  FontStyle bold
  FontSize 13
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #D6B656
  FontSize 11
}

' ---------- the store, its terminals and the people -------------------------
class Store {
  storeId
  name
  address
}

class Register {
  registerId
}

class "Cashier\n(role of person)" as Cashier {
  cashierId
  name
}

class "Customer\n(role of person)" as Customer {
  customerId
  name
}

' ---------- the transactions: business transactions come first --------------
class Sale {
  dateTime
  isComplete
}

class ReturnTransaction {
  dateTime
  reason
  refundTotal
}

' ---------- transaction line items ------------------------------------------
class SalesLineItem {
  quantity
}

class ReturnLineItem {
  quantity
  resellable
}

' ---------- products: description first, then catalogue ---------------------
class "ProductSpecification\n(description)" as ProductSpecification {
  itemID
  description
  price
  taxRate
}

class ProductCatalog

class Item {
  serialNumber
}

' ---------- payments ---------------------------------------------------------
abstract class Payment {
  amount
  dateTime
}

class CashPayment {
  amountTendered
  changeDue
}

class CreditPayment {
  cardNumber
  authorizationCode
}

' ---------- the report of a sale --------------------------------------------
class Receipt {
  receiptId
  dateTime
  total
}

' ===========================================================================
' associations
' ===========================================================================
Store "1" -- "1..*" Register : houses >
Register "1" -- "0..1" Sale : records >
Register "1" -- "1" ProductCatalog : uses >

Cashier "1" -- "0..*" Sale : is operated by >
Customer "0..1" -- "0..*" Sale : buys >
Customer "0..1" -- "0..*" ReturnTransaction : returns >

' composition: a line item cannot outlive its transaction (Creator, too)
Sale "1" *-- "1..*" SalesLineItem : contains >
ReturnTransaction "1" *-- "1..*" ReturnLineItem : contains >

SalesLineItem "0..*" -- "1" ProductSpecification : describes >
ReturnLineItem "0..*" -- "1" ProductSpecification : describes >

ProductSpecification "1" -- "0..*" Item : describes >
ProductCatalog "1" -- "0..*" ProductSpecification : contains >

' a sale may be paid by more than one payment (part cash, part card)
Sale "1" -- "1..*" Payment : is paid by >
ReturnTransaction "1" -- "0..1" Payment : is reimbursed by >

Payment <|-- CashPayment
Payment <|-- CreditPayment

Sale "1" -- "0..1" Receipt : is recorded on >
ReturnTransaction "0..*" -- "0..1" Sale : reverses >

note right of ProductSpecification
  **Description class** (Item-Descriptor pattern).
  Records price/description of a *kind* of product,
  independent of whether any Item currently exists,
  so the price survives the stock selling out.
  See Applying UML and Patterns, section 9.13.
end note

note bottom of ReturnLineItem
  **resellable** is a real domain notion, not a
  software flag: damaged goods are not put back
  on the shelf, so the stock-on-hand the shop
  needs differs from the quantity refunded.
end note

note left of Payment
  Polymorphic payment.  CashPayment and
  CreditPayment settle differently, but a Sale
  only needs to know it has a Payment.
end note

@enduml
